Experimental, NOT landed: one bulk read per RLE bitmap record instead of
three SDL_RW calls per row.

Measured no change: 24614 ms of bitmap parse either way, three runs each.
It does cut ~100,000 SDL calls to ~1,300 and costs no permanent RAM, and it
carries the per-row path as a validated fallback, so it may be worth having
on hardware if the cost profile there is different. Bounds come from the
bitmap offset table the way unpack_collection() does it: next offset as the
end, src_length as the sentinel for the last.

Apply with: git apply tools/patches/experimental-rle-single-read.patch

diff --git a/Source_Files/Misc/shapes_sdl.cpp b/Source_Files/Misc/shapes_sdl.cpp
index 0a46ded..7763356 100644
